  "claims": [
    "The four beta projection argument diagrams are extended to arbitrary finite pure wire proof paths, including formal inverses. The erased branch cases are derived recursively without a whole-track generator.",
    "When both fork components change along actual paths, projecting with fst and then beta agrees with beta followed by the first path; snd selects the second path. All of these comparisons use only the previous old pure local argument/groupoid library.",
    "In the retained pure Fin 31 extension, assembling two supplied projected paths by inverse eta and fork has actual higher projection laws: projecting the assembled path and beta gives back the corresponding supplied path.",
    "The actual existing identityNormal(pair a b) path is compared with that eta assembly, removing only a zero-step bookkeeping prefix. Both product shapes a and b are arbitrary.",
    "Consequently, postcomposing the actual product identity normalization with fst/snd and then the beta of its canonical components is compared with leftId of that projection followed by the actual existing projectLeft/projectRight(identityNormal child) path.",
    "The existing public normalizeCell(identity a) endpoint transport is definitionally equal to identityNormal a, proved by rfl. Both product projection squares are exported for this PUBLIC normalizer, not a replacement normalization algorithm.",
    "The existing MAC presentation embeds both actual public normalizer projection squares with empty pure support. No new basic higher diagram family, basis or first-level rule is introduced.",
    "The concrete sampled context executes one MAC.before stage and copies its full output before applying the identity-normalization/projection comparison. Its exact condition support is singleton stage. Repaired joint equality in the updated checked model retains the correlated past, state and input."
  ],
  "finite_scope": {
    "unchanged_pure_schematic_tag_count": 31,
    "new_basic_generator_families": 0,
    "path_naturality_inputs": "Actual arbitrary finite paths of the eighteen pure Cartesian rules, including inverses; not conditional crypto rewrite paths",
    "normalizer_inputs": "Identity at pair(a,b), with arbitrary product shapes a and b; the supplied projectLeft and projectRight paths retain recursive identityNormal child computations",
    "public_normalizer": "The existing frozen normalizeCell, with an explicit identity transport equality, not a new normalization function",
    "mixed_context": "MAC.before stage, full-output copy, identity of the pair, and fst; no before/after crypto rewrite"
  },
  "limits": [
    "These are actual product identity/projection normalization squares. They do not yet compare the full existing componentThenCanonical and direct tensor normalization paths.",
    "The selector/lift routing compatibility, substitution unit/associativity comparisons, and normalization idempotence as higher proofs remain to be supplied.",
    "No complete finite higher basis or arbitrary branching classifier for the whole eighteen-root/mixed catalogue is established.",
    "Erased-branch naturality concerns pure proof paths. Conditional requirements of the sampled crypto prefix are retained and rechecked, not discarded.",
    "No total certificate size, checker runtime advantage, code-changing reduction, loss/time/resource bound or full physical oracle/keygen execution is proved. Unregistered NativeConfiguredMAC integration remains excluded.",
    "Mathematical novelty remains unconfirmed. Generic beta/eta coherence or product reconstruction is not claimed as a new abstract principle. No new external primary-source reading or independent review occurred."
  ],
  "next_obligations": [
    "Construct actual commuting squares between liftLeft/liftRight and selectNormal for typed slots, using the distribution/projection diagrams and categorical coherence.",
